 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.38,
   "text": "Lately, everyone's been obsessed with writing the perfect hook, but they're forgetting that each"
  },
  {
   "start": 4.38,
   "end": 9.12,
   "text": "hook has two parts, and your content is probably forgetting one of them. Welcome to Content Camp,"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.32,
   "end": 13.82,
   "text": "your eight-week crash course in storytelling, filming, and editing so that by the end of"
  },
  {
   "start": 13.82,
   "end": 17.98,
   "text": "the summer, you'll be creating content that actually performs. If we break down the anatomy"
  },
  {
   "start": 17.98,
   "end": 22.74,
   "text": "of a great video, you'll see that there are almost always two parts. The visual hook,"
  },
  {
   "start": 22.86,
   "end": 26.6,
   "text": "which is what people see, and the verbal hook, which is what people hear. It's estimated"
  },
  {
   "start": 26.6,
   "end": 33.3,
   "text": "that 80 to 85% of social media is consumed without sound, and even when the sound is on,"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.46,
   "end": 37.38,
   "text": "people are usually only half listening. What this means is that your visual hook has to"
  },
  {
   "start": 37.38,
   "end": 42.14,
   "text": "land with no audio, and your verbal hook has to land with no visual. If either of those depend on"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.14,
   "end": 46.02,
   "text": "the other to make sense, then you've already lost the great majority of your audience."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.22,
   "end": 50.42,
   "text": "The biggest mistake I see when it comes to hooks are when both hooks say the same thing."
  },
  {
   "start": 50.54,
   "end": 54.92,
   "text": "So for example, let's say you're filming a workday in my life vlog, and you do your morning"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.92,
   "end": 58.54,
   "text": "routine, then you commute to the office, then you get to the office, and you start your work."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.66,
   "end": 63.0,
   "text": "If your voiceover just narrates what you're doing on screen, then it's not as engaging for the viewer,"
  },
  {
   "start": 63.02,
   "end": 67.98,
   "text": "and instead you want them to do different jobs. So for example, you could say something like,"
  },
  {
   "start": 68.18,
   "end": 74.02,
   "text": "I deleted my first 100 videos before I ever posted my first, or this is how Blank got me"
  },
  {
   "start": 74.02,
   "end": 78.2,
   "text": "my dream job, and you can insert something crazy or captivating. That way your visuals"
  },
  {
   "start": 78.2,
   "end": 82.3,
   "text": "give context, but the main focus is the story that you're trying to tell. A few hook"
  },
  {
   "start": 82.3,
   "end": 87.34,
   "text": "formulas we found the most success with are the bold claim, the result, and the call out."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.78,
   "end": 91.98,
   "text": "But if you want our full hook breakdown with specific examples you can implement into your"
  },
  {
   "start": 91.98,
   "end": 95.84,
   "text": "own content, then you can comment camper and I'll send it straight to your email inbox."
  },
  {
   "start": 96.18,
   "end": 100.1,
   "text": "Next week, we're going to get behind the camera to talk about equipment essentials you need to"
  },
  {
   "start": 100.1,
   "end": 102.28,
   "text": "create the absolute best quality of content."
  }
 ]
}